course: dictionary
lesson: 8908
title: Shy: nervous, quiet, or keeping away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shy means feeling nervous and quiet with people you do not know well. Look at the clues in «A girl in Leeds would not greet or answer her new teacher for weeks because she was shy.» She stayed quiet because she felt nervous with someone new. Shy is not the same as rude. It is about feeling scared to join in.
explain: Shy can describe animals too. The text says «the truth is shy piranhas», so the films got it wrong. Shy animals are easily frightened and keep away from people, so you must be quiet to see them.
explain: Shy has more meanings. To shy away from something means to avoid it because you feel nervous. A horse may shy and jump suddenly when it is frightened. Shy of a number means a little less than it, so «just shy of ten» means nearly ten, but not quite.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If Filip is shy and quiet, the rest of the sentence fits. If you swap in a word like loud, the meaning breaks, and that tells you shy is the right fit.
fact: Shy means nervous and quiet with people you do not know well.
fact: A shy animal is easily frightened and keeps away from people.
fact: To shy away from something means to avoid it because you are nervous.
fact: «Just shy of» a number means a little less than it, as in «just shy of ten».
fact: Shy has other forms too: shyer and shyest, or shier and shiest.
exercise: «A girl in Leeds would not greet or answer her new teacher for weeks because she was shy.» Why did she stay quiet? | She was angry at her teacher | She did not know how to write | She was tired and sleepy | *She was nervous with someone new
exercise: «Many wild animals are shy, so you must be quiet to see them.» What does shy mean here? | Very fast at running | Hungry all the time | *Easily frightened and keeps away from people | Very loud and friendly
exercise: The jug holds just shy of one litre. What does just shy of mean? | *A little less than one litre | A lot more than one litre | Exactly one litre | Empty
test: Sam did not want to put his hand up, so he began to shy away from the question. What does shy away mean? | Run around the room | Ask the question loudly | Answer it at once with a joke | *Avoid it because he feels nervous
test: The horse began to shy at the loud bang. What does shy mean here? | Eat its food quickly | Sit down and rest | *Jump suddenly because it is frightened | Walk slowly and carefully to the barn
exam: Ella says the tower is just shy of 100 metres tall. What does she mean? | It is well over 200 metres | It is exactly 100 metres | It is made of soft wood | *It is a little under 100 metres
